   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 3 of the laws of 2020 relating to establishing the\nstretch limousine passenger safety task force, in relation to extending the\ndate the final report shall be issued and in relation to extending the\neffectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7563",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7563-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1 & 2, Chap 3 of 2020",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7563\n\nSPONSOR: KAPLAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 3 of the laws of 2020 relating to establishing\nthe stretch limousine passenger safety task force, in relation to\nextending the date the final report shall be issued and in relation to\nextending the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo extend the due date for the stretch limousine passenger safety task\nforce report.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends subdivision 8 of chapter 3 of the laws of 2020 to\nprovide that the stretch limousine passenger safety task force shall\nissue its final report no later than October 1, 2022.\n\nSection two provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapter 3 of 2020 created the Stretch Limousine Passenger Safety Task\nForce, which is charged with conducting a comprehensive review of\nmatters influencing the safety, adequacy, efficiency and reliability of\nstretch limousine transportation. The Task Force was supposed to issue\nits final report and recommendations to the Governor and to the Legisla-\nture by November 1, 2021. It was also required to hold at least one\npublic hearing to solicit public comments prior to issuing its report.\n\nThe deadline has now passed, without the release of the report. This\nbill extends the deadline for issuance of the Task Force's final report\nto October 1, 2022. This will allow the Task Force sufficient time to\nconvene, hold a public hearing and produce a thorough report and recom-\nmendations. Furthermore, this deadline will ensure that the report is\ncompleted prior to the fourth anniversary of the tragic Schoharie crash.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATION:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall be deemed to have been\nin full force and effect on and after November 1, 2021.\n",
